Negative control for the guest link-visit record's draw-at-boot declaration
(R-GUEST, RT3).

`useAffiliateLinkVisit` holds nothing before its first `visit()` — its one
context key, `target`, is empty until a visit resolves. The record declares
`drawsEmpty` so the surface draws its Record visit control at boot. This mutant
drops the flag from the DECLARATION: the runtime is intact, but the page reads
the empty record as a load and sits on a skeleton, so the visit that would end
the load can never be made.

Apply from the repo root: `git apply <this file>`; revert with `git apply -R`.

Expected red (module lane): record-archetype-routing.spec.ts once it covers the
guest visit declaration — `presentation.record.drawsEmpty` must be true for a
manager that publishes no record before its first write.

